- NullPointerException if schemaUri is null and enableSchemaCache true: because schemaCache.get(null) allowed? ConcurrentHashMap permits null key? No, ConcurrentHashMap does NOT allow null keys or values; get(null) throws NullPointerException. So NPE at schemaCache.get(schemaUri). Also later getMappedSchema(null, config) may also NPE. So need test for null schemaUri with cache enabled.

- NullPointerException if config is null? cachedUriSchema.withConfig(null) could cause NPE inside withConfig if not handling null. But we don't know implementation; but we can test that it doesn't throw NPE (maybe already covered). Already existing test for null config when cache enabled expects no NPE. So fine.

- IllegalStateException if schemaCache.put(schemaUri, null) not allowed; but code checks null before put, so safe.

- Potential exception from getMappedSchema throwing runtime exception (e.g., IOException). But method signature doesn't declare throws, so getMappedSchema may throw unchecked exceptions. Could be NullPointerException inside getMappedSchema due to invalid URI format. So test scenario where getMappedSchema throws an unchecked exception; loadSchema should propagate it.

