Thus we need to identify exception scenarios not covered: NullPointerException when schemaUri null with cache enabled; NullPointerException when getMappedSchema returns null with cache enabled; RuntimeException propagation from getMappedSchema; IllegalArgumentException if schemaUri is malformed? Not in method.

Also potential ConcurrentModification? Not.

Thus we create new test groups:

- Cache enabled – null schemaUri -> expect NPE.

- Cache enabled – getMappedSchema returns null -> expect NPE (since withConfig called on null). Already there is a test for cache enabled – cache miss, mapping returns null expecting null. That may be inaccurate; we need to add exception scenario.

- Cache enabled – getMappedSchema throws unchecked exception (e.g., IllegalStateException) -> expect same exception propagated.

- Cache disabled – getMappedSchema throws unchecked exception -> expect same exception.

- Cache disabled – schemaUri null -> already covered (NPE). Already test case exists for cache disabled – null schemaUri. So fine.

- Cache disabled – config null? getMappedSchema may handle null; not exception.

